{"id": "EUVD-2026-106918", "enisaUuid": "5056b687-fa28-3c75-890f-9df4acf4d3b8", "description": "Vyper 0.3.8 through 0.5.0b1 contains a compiler miscompilation vulnerability in parse_IfExp that reads nested arrays with narrower inner bounds using the wider result type's memory layout. When a ternary selects the narrower array, inner arrays after the first are read at wrong offsets, causing contracts to silently store corrupted values or revert.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:49:19", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/security/advisories/GHSA-cw3h-xwxq-8cx2", "https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/commit/1fb7dfe2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vyper-0.3.8-through-0.5-0b1-memory-misread-via-ternary-nested-array-selection"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114115", "GHSA-fccw-crcx-53fr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4fbe63fc-c13e-39da-8777-15bdcf2fd1fb", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.3.8 \u22640.5.0b1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "05eb99b7-c0d3-3db7-936b-8b94dd13191b", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}], "isExploited": false}